Subject: [PATCH 1/6] feat(summary): port the isopsephy card from the old
 estate and add qabalah

The old agent's /summary card is ported byte-identical as gateway/summary_card.py,
so the founder's historical readings do not move. Faithfulness is proved by
differential replay against the old implementation, not asserted: 18,125 renders
over 669 inputs x 9 renderers, 0 differences.

gateway/qabalah.py is the new half, and it is stdlib-only:

- Greek isopsephy with all 27 letters. The old card had no Greek at all, so
  Ihsous=888 and cxs=666 were unreachable. Digamma, koppa and sampi are what
  make 999 reachable; without them the series stops at 800.
- Hebrew gematria over Hebrew script, mispar hechrechi and mispar gadol.
  The old card ran a "Hebrew" cipher over A-Z that wrapped after 22 letters,
  so W scored the same as A. That defect is left in place in summary_card.py
  because the differential replay depends on it, and it is named in an
  incident test.
- The Tree: 10 sephirot and the 22 paths with their Golden Dawn trumps, so a
  Hebrew word shows the paths it walks.
- Equivalences over a 37-word canon. No value is stored anywhere, only words
  and glosses, so the tables are the only authority and cannot drift from it.
- A daily game. The target is drawn from the canon by date ordinal, so it is
  always reachable and nothing is persisted.

Rungs, per the testing ladder in AGENTS.md:
  rung 2  properties over the ciphers and the tables (12)
  rung 3  differential replay against the old implementation, skipped when
          the old tree is absent, deleted when the old estate is retired
  rung 4  one incident test, test_incident_w_scored_the_same_as_a_in_the_
          old_hebrew_cipher
No rung 1 example tests were written.

/summary is Slack-via-/hermes only. The registry was already at exactly the
50-slash cap, so a native slot would have silently clamped /insights off the
end. The new command takes the /hermes route and the live Slack surface does
not move.

Crew DECISIONS entry 6 discontinues Hermes, so qabalah.py also runs as a bare
pair of files with no gateway around it.

